<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

Pick a value from a list you can filter by typing - one, several (chips), or a new one.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/combobox)

<%= embed UI::ComboboxPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Combobox(items: frameworks, name: "framework", default_value: "Astro") do
  ComboboxInput(placeholder: "Search a framework")
  ComboboxContent do
    ComboboxEmpty { "No frameworks found." }
    ComboboxList { |item| ComboboxItem(value: item) { item } }
  end
end
```

The sibling of [Autocomplete](<%= page_path(:autocomplete) %>) - it shares its parts and filtering - for **picking a
value**: the value is always one of the items, the input shows its label and reverts to it when you leave, and
hidden inputs submit it under `name:`. Object items are read through `item_to_string_value:` and
`item_to_string_label:`. The chevron is on by default. For a short list without search, use a
[Select](<%= page_path(:select) %>).

